# Post-pivot mount table for the QEMU UFS root: `/` is the mounted UFS2 disk.
# The bootstrap initfs table still starts with initfs: before the pivot; the UFS
# payload ships this file so `mount` and `df` report UFS on `/`.

/ ufs:
/tmp ramfs:
/dev/null null:
/dev/zero zero:
/dev/random rand:
/dev/urandom rand:
